Spec: Select Tool

Purpose:
  Primary interaction tool for selecting, moving, resizing, and rotating shapes.

Owns:
  ./select.ts
  ./select.test.ts

Must:
  Click selects the topmost shape under cursor.
  Click on empty area deselects all.
  Shift+click adds/removes from multi-selection.
  Drag from empty area starts rubber-band selection.
  Right-to-left drag uses crossing selection (partial overlap).
  Left-to-right drag uses enclosing selection (fully inside).
  Drag on selected shape moves all selected shapes.
  Drag resize handles scales selected shapes.
  Drag rotation handle rotates selected shapes around center.
  Snap to grid/endpoints/midpoints when snapping is enabled.
  All moves/resizes/rotations are undoable via commands.

Must not:
  Modify shape data directly — must use MoveShapeCommand, ResizeShapeCommand, RotateShapeCommand.
  Create new shapes.
  Trigger unnecessary re-renders during drag (use restore-from-snapshot pattern).

Depends on:
  @MoveShapeCommand
  @ResizeShapeCommand
  @RotateShapeCommand
  @captureSnapshot
  @restoreSnapshot
  @SnapManager

Scenario: click to select
  Given 2 shapes on canvas and nothing selected
  When the user clicks on shape A
  Then shape A is selected
  And shape B is not selected

Scenario: rubber-band enclosing selection
  Given 3 shapes on canvas
  When the user drags left-to-right enclosing shapes A and B
  Then shapes A and B are selected
  And shape C (outside the rectangle) is not selected

Scenario: move with undo
  Given shape A is selected at position (100, 100)
  When the user drags shape A to (150, 120)
  Then shape A is at (150, 120)
  When the user presses Ctrl+Z
  Then shape A is back at (100, 100)

Tasks:
  [x] Click selection.
  [x] Multi-selection with shift.
  [x] Rubber-band selection (enclosing and crossing).
  [x] Move shapes with snap.
  [x] Resize via 8 handles.
  [x] Rotate via rotation handle.
  [x] Undo/redo for all transforms.
